ks don't  sell right so instead of setting up your  own book store buying the wrong books  and spending all this money you can  quickly test with pretty low cost way  and it's a plus for the retailer because  they can get new people coming into  their store it works better when it's a  smaller retailer small output that  you're working with  and hopefully you can set up these types  of profit or relationships to test your  concept the second thing I would do is  try to partner up with other  organizations that may not be retail  operations but also serve your same  target market so if you're selling  religious books partner up with  different churches if you're selling  books about coffee partner up with  different cafes and again offered to  sell books within their establishment  give them a little bit of the profit and  you're going to help drive people to  learn more about their organization I  get how lets you test to see if the  model works or not and you not you're  not out a lot of money to set up that  type of business the last thing I would  do is with retail operations it's really  important to get the location right  right you can spend a lot of money  sitting up your bookstore but it's in  the wrong location even if you have the  right books you're not going to be able  to turn a profit so it's really good to  be able to test different locations to  see which one works before you commit a  lot of money to set up your bookstore so  what I would try to do is set up  partnerships with different retailers  and different locations to see what  works and what doesn't work you can also  have book sale days and set up you know  outside different stores just for one  time and see if it works see if you're  able to draw people see if it's the  right type of demographic that you want  to target or not and it's a quick way  again the test to see if you're  attracting the right people are not  before you go out and invest all that  money into creating the bookstore but by  doing all these little things I partner  with different organizations you're able  to test see what works what books people  like what location works start building  up a list of customers people who like  you know you want to buy more from you  and you have money that starts to come  in which then you can use to go on  actually create your book store and if  you do decide to go and try to get  investment at this point you have some  traction you have some momentum you have  something behind you more than just an  idea and it'll be a lot easier to go  upgrades that happily looking for so I  hope that helps Santosh if you guys  liked the video please give it a thumbs  up below and I'd also love to hear your  thoughts and feedback if you want to  leave a comment under the video and stay  tuned for the next episode  you
 

